<article class="env-proposition" id="00GQ">
<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/00GQ">Proposition <span data-tag="00GQ">1.2.1.19</span>.</a> Let $S_{}$ be a simplicial set and let $u: S_{} \rightarrow \underline{ \pi _0( S_{})}_{}$ be the component map of Construction <a data-tag="00GP" href="/tag/00GP">1.2.1.18</a>. For every set $J$, composition with $u$ induces a bijection </p>
<div class="equation">
  \[  \operatorname{Hom}_{\operatorname{Set}}( \pi _0(S_{}), J ) \rightarrow \operatorname{Hom}_{\operatorname{Set_{\Delta }}}( S_{}, \underline{J}_{} ). \]
</div>
</article><article class="env-proof">
<p>
<strong>Proof.</strong>
      Decomposing $S_{}$ as the union of its connected components, we can reduce to the case where $S_{}$ is connected, in which case the desired result is a reformulation of Corollary <a data-tag="00GH" href="/tag/00GH">1.2.1.12</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
</p>
</article>
